			<div class="content" id="post-content-1504645">
									

<p>My conceptual problems with this piece still stand. The long version of my complaints was lost when the prior version was deleted, but in brief:</p>
<ul>
<li>The internal coverup is nonsensical and counterproductive. Intentional misinformation within the Foundation is expensive and dangerous for anything short of an infohazard, with rare exceptions like the Fountain of Youth; using it here is excessive and unjustified.</li>
<li>Setting aside the coverup, the only thing that this artifact does is pump out reality shifts (CK-class scenarios by my interpretation). Like any K-class scenario, CK events are only an interesting device when employed as a means to an end. A machine that triggers nonspecific XK events would make a boring SCP. This thing does nothing but trigger nonspecific CK events, to the same effect.</li>
</ul>
<p>The writing is solid, the concept bugs the hell out of me. Downvote.</p>

